    {
      "id": "b9f45ec111f412da488d3a450f2d3544ab794f31",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 443919477,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Hi,\nWould it make sense to use a presized array instead and possibly conbert that to a value_string_ext?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6792385,
            "username": "AndersBroman",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "AndersBroman",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/132fb48f26018ea9516aea909144af3c3a94eaf2ba477efaa9a232abe80d322c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/AndersBroman"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-11-09T08:52:14.433Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-11-09T08:52:14.433Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 77231368,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 879,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "348abfb58a9b1dbcb7ae6229c25f12aad436635e",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 443957905,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I did think about using a pre-sized array, then we could either use value_string_ext(), or even just a direct array lookup.  The good thing about an array is that we could replace the g_strdup() call (2.86% of whole run in my profile) with g_strlcpy().  The downsides of this are sizing:\n\n- several items get added each week (currently at 56552 entries).  Could possibly get tools/sminmpec.pl to write out the size to a #define in a header file?\n\n- enterprises.tsv has some pretty long lines, so making each entry as long as the longest would waste a lot of memory. Maybe we could store all of the entries in one large buffer and have the table lookup return an index.  Again, maybe tools/sminmpec.pl could help size that buffer\n\nThe other optimisation opportunity could be avoiding the call to ws_strtou32() (2.97% of whole run in my profile).  It looks as though the number usually (always?) increases by 1 with no gaps.  If we kept a running total and efficiently compared the number we have with what is expected, and only call w_strtou32() if they differed, I believe most of this time would be saved.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/030414c33f619ee28811cd9c073802ef2267d160ab2744eb8427bd49af4c7998?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/martin.r.mathieson"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-11-09T09:44:41.030Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-11-09T09:44:41.030Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 77231368,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 879,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "8f19b1f471e0f15b4da69773cdead29bf56a7e03",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 443964174,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Hi,\nWell the simplest/most efficient would probably be to let tools/sminmpec.pl create the value_string_ext in a file and use that. I think we used to have a manually created one :-)\n\n/Anders",
          "author": {
            "id": 6792385,
